{"at": "2026-11-24T09:06:24Z", "class": ["method"], "evidence": ["gate:checks"], "id": "f8172ff337c52632", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "rework", "text": "A ledger check made of a test runner and a file name passes when that file is missing, because the runner skips what it cannot find. Two requirements were marked done that way. Write such checks so that they fail when the named test does not exist, for example by testing for the file first.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T09:06:24Z", "class": ["method"], "evidence": ["gate:checks"], "id": "4b7ea87679ad8ee6", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "first-success", "text": "A long design document prepared by an assistant and labelled fully verified held 22 contradicted and 132 unsupported claims among 292 graded. Keep such a document word for word as the source, grade it in parallel by subject against cited sources, and build the product's data only from the graded version, with a short review that says what holds, what is wrong and what the product does about it.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T09:06:24Z", "class": ["method"], "evidence": ["gate:checks"], "id": "1c0b3ed86663a5fa", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "first-success", "text": "A watchlist received from the owner (things that must not appear) became a test that scans every text the product shows; within the hour it caught an error in data written by the lead. Turn watchlists into tests on the day they arrive.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T09:06:25Z", "class": ["method"], "evidence": ["gate:checks"], "id": "25f64b449c638f2c", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "owner-correction", "text": "When the owner stops a background helper, do not start it again unasked: finish the rest, keep what it would have checked out of the product, say plainly that it is not done, and ask once whether to run it.", "trust": "observed"}
